the choice of that)TjT* -0.176 Tc (revenue instrument. Decentralization of control and lower toll collection costs are)TjT* -0.098 Tc (identified as conditions under which tolls would more likely become the preferred)TjT* 0 Tc (revenue instrument for highways.)TjETendstreamendobj11 0 obj2270endobj4 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 5 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F1 6 0 R /F2 7 0 R /F3 8 0 R /F4 9 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 10 0 R>>endobj13 0 obj<</Length 14 0 R>>stream
BT/F1 12 Tf321.5 45 TD (2)Tj/F3 14 Tf-213 663 TD 1.25 Tc 0 Tw (1.)Tj13 0 TD ( )Tj7 0 TD 0.416 Tc (INTRODUCTION)Tj/F1 12 Tf16 -20 TD -0.121 Tc (Cordon tolls are becoming a popular method of restricting traffic in cities and)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.057 Tc (financing new infrastructure.  Singapore, Oslo, Trondheim, and Bergen are cities with)Tj0 -18 TD -0.082 Tc (such a mechanism in place.  Imperfect cordons, such as a toll barrier on a major highway)TjT* -0.112 Tc (with toll-free entrance and exit ramps, have traditionally been used both in the early days of)TjT* -0.074 Tc (turnpikes and more recently on some limited access highway systems.  In both cases, local)TjT* -0.059 Tc (trips \(which remain within the cordon\) do not pay tolls, while through trips \(which cross)TjT* -0.087 Tc (the cordon\) do.  On the other hand, tax financing has been common both historically)TjT* (\(initially the tax was in terms of labor\), and more recently for local roads, which are funded)TjT* -0.07 Tc (through general revenues. Taxes also rely on a cordon, the boundary of the relevant)TjT* -0.036 Tc (jurisdiction, within which they are assessed.)Tj36 -18 TD -0.097 Tc (In this paper a model of network financing is developed which incorporates the)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.093 Tc (basic features of the economic structure of transportation networks.  It includes the demand)Tj0 -18 TD -0.084 Tc (and supply interaction, the choices available to actors \(consumers and producers\), and the)TjT* -0.089 Tc (linkage between the two when the network is locally owned by the residents of its)TjT* -0.113 Tc (jurisdiction.  The idea of decentralized, local control and multiple jurisdictions distinguishes)TjT* -0.111 Tc (this analysis from one where a central authority maximizes global welfare. The model\325s)TjT* -0.097 Tc (theoretical results should be consistent with what is empirically known about network)TjT* -0.077 Tc (financing.  It should thus describe what network financing choices are made under various)TjT* -0.121 Tc (circumstances.  Policies can then be drafted which alter circumstances to affect the desired)TjT* -0.109 Tc (choice of financing mechanism.)Tj36 -18 TD -0.12 Tc (The main complication is the joint production and consumption of the key good)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.077 Tc (\(network services\) by the jurisdiction and its residents.  The network operator \(jurisdiction\))Tj0 -18 TD -0.103 Tc (makes the network available while residents consume the network for traveling. Spatial)TjT* -0.118 Tc (complexity in this problem results from the fact that jurisdiction residents use both local and)TjT* -0.075 Tc (non-local networks, and each jurisdiction\325s network is used by both local and non-local)TjT* -0.091 Tc (residents.  The network is not perfectly competitive and thus retains some monopoly)TjT* -0.102 Tc (power.  The degree of locality in the use of the network directly shapes the local welfare)TjT* -0.099 Tc (resulting from a particular revenue mechanism, and itself is a function of jurisdiction size.)TjT* -0.097 Tc (The choice of financing instrument must trade off the number of spatial free riders, system)TjT* -0.074 Tc (users who don\325t pay their cost because of the location, and the costs of collection. The)TjT* -0.118 Tc (price charged for a given instrument is limited by the elasticity of demand on those who are)TjT* 0 Tc (charged.)Tj36 -18 TD -0.093 Tc (The central thesis argues that, since jurisdictions try to do well by their residents)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.087 Tc (who are both voters and travelers, the effects of a revenue instrument on local residents is a)Tj0 -18 TD -0.104 Tc (key consideration in the choice of that revenue instrument. It is assumed that jurisdictions)TjETendstreamendobj14 0 obj3754endobj12 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 5 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F1 6 0 R /F3 8 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 13 0 R>>endobj16 0 obj<</Length 17 0 R>>stream
