roportion to use.  In realistic)TjT* -0.101 Tc (situations of highway transportation, there are transaction costs involved in collecting)TjT* -0.137 Tc (revenue, which dictate that a complete and perfect revenue instrument is not available on)TjT* 0 Tc (every link. )Tj72 0 TD -0.089 Tc (It is an assumption of this work that jurisdictions would rather place the)Tj-72 -18 TD -0.102 Tc (burden of financing on non-local travelers in order to maximize local welfare.  Therefore,)Tj0 -18 TD -0.115 Tc (in the case of local control there is a preference to tax through trips and exempt trips which)TjT* -0.107 Tc (both originate in and are destined for the jurisdiction \(locals\), thereby allowing locals to be)TjT* (the free rider. At the extreme case, that of a single short road segment \(a near perfect)TjT* -0.114 Tc (cordon\), this approaches the efficient revenue instrument of tolling nearly all travelers in)TjT* -0.029 Tc (proportion to use, as there are very few, if any, \322locals\323.  However if those who make)TjT* -0.107 Tc (through trips control the political process, or through trips are really \322local\323 because the)TjT* -0.091 Tc (road authority has a broad geographical scope,  then taxes may be preferred because of)TjT* -0.053 Tc (their lower transactions costs.)Tj36 -18 TD -0.11 Tc (This hypothesis does not claim to be a total explanation under all circumstances, as)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.092 Tc (a socio-political system like infrastructure financing has many influences. For instance,)Tj0 -18 TD -0.115 Tc (perfect excludability on roads coupled with the presence of \322free\323 alternatives, reductions in)TjT* -0.091 Tc (toll collection costs, and private ownership, may all increase the willingness of a)TjT* -0.124 Tc (jurisdiction to tolerate tolls even on local residents.  The socio-economic level of the)TjETendstreamendobj17 0 obj3863endobj15 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 5 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F1 6 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Conte