BT/F1 12 Tf321.5 45 TD (4)Tj-213 666 TD -0.082 Tc 0 Tw (jurisdiction may influence its willingness to adopt congestion pricing.  Further, the)Tj0 -18 TD -0.109 Tc (influence of key players in business and politics with specific preferences are unpredictable)TjT* -0.12 Tc (and may greatly shape the decisions made over time.  Another factor is the prevailing)TjT* -0.061 Tc (ideology of government.  In the 18th and 19th centuries, a philosophy of limited,)TjT* -0.113 Tc (decentralized government, or )Tj/F4 12 Tf140 0 TD -0.205 Tc (laissez faire)Tj/F1 12 Tf55 0 TD -0.088 Tc (, was conducive to private enterprise at all levels,)Tj-195 -18 TD -0.083 Tc (including roads.  However, this philosophy declined in America in the twentieth century, at)Tj0 -18 TD -0.081 Tc (least through the early 1970\325s.  Finally, regional rivalry and the idea of progress certainly)TjT* -0.078 Tc (have their place, promoting one-upmanship and construction for the sake of construction.)Tj36 -18 TD -0.088 Tc (The model presented in this paper provides a strategic framework for assessing the)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.118 Tc (outcome of alternative revenue instruments. This paper examines the free rider problem in)Tj0 -18 TD -0.134 Tc (relation to transaction \(toll collection\) costs. This model explicitly compares the welfare)TjT* -0.092 Tc (associated with taxes and those associated with tolls on a simplified network with various)TjT* -0.111 Tc (jurisdiction sizes. The actions available to network operators  and the posited objectives that)TjT* -0.058 Tc (the two main sets of actors, the network operator \(owned by residents\) and travelers, are)TjT* -0.065 Tc (presented.  Then, the network geometry of this model is illustrated.  The model of flow as)TjT* -0.063 Tc (a function of trip length and tolls is explained, as is the resultant consumers\325 surplus.)TjT* -0.094 Tc (Profit calculations, and their component cost and revenue equations are presented.  The)TjT* -0.116 Tc (models are then evaluated using assumed parameters to better understand its implication.)TjT* -0.054 Tc (Finally, key points, some policy conclusions, and directions for future research are)TjT* 0 Tc (summarized.)Tj/F3 14 Tf0 -21 TD 1.25 Tc (2.)Tj13 0 TD ( )Tj7 0 TD 0.508 Tc (ACTIONS AND OBJECTIVES)Tj/F1 12 Tf16 -20 TD -0.091 Tc (A jurisdiction is defined as the owner of the road authority responsible for)Tj-36 -18 TD -0.059 Tc (maintaining the road. These jurisdictions, or network operators, have several classes of)Tj0 -18 TD -0.087 Tc (actions, this research focuses on selecting a revenue instrument \(taxes or tolls\) and price or)TjT* -0.135 Tc (rate \(collectively called revenue mechanism\). Broadly, the two available revenue)Tj0 -22 TD -0.053 Tc (instruments are taxes and tolls. As used here, a )Tj/F4 12 Tf225 0 TD -0.25 Tc (toll)Tj/F1 12 Tf15 0 TD -0.088 Tc (  \(denoted by the Tau symbol \()Tj/F5 12 Tf145 0 TD (t)Tj/F1 12 Tf5 0 TD 0 Tc (\)\) is a)Tj-390 -22 TD -0.095 Tc (fixed sum of money charged for a specific service or privilege \(for instance, the right to)Tj0 -18 TD -0.096 Tc (travel on a link or subnetwork\). Our toll is a fee levied by the road authority as travelers)Tj0 -22 TD 0 Tc (cross a cordon.  In contrast, the term )Tj/F4 12 Tf177 0 TD (tax)Tj/F1 12 Tf14 0 TD -0.077 Tc (  \(denoted by the Chi symbol \()Tj/F5 12 Tf144 0 TD (c)Tj/F1 12 Tf7 0 TD -0.072 Tc (\)\) is defined as a)Tj-342 -22 TD (fixed sum of money charged for a general service or privilege, such as the support of)Tj0 -18 TD -0.061 Tc (government or roads in general, independent of use. Our tax is a periodic \(e.g. annual\) fee)TjT* -0.104 Tc (levied by a jurisdiction on its residents in the form of a poll tax.  The distinction between a)TjT* -0.09 Tc (tax and a toll is in how specific or general the service is which is being provided and how)TjT* -0.1 Tc (closely it aligns with the revenue mechanism.  Thus, a gas tax is more like a toll than a)TjT* -0.06